# The bytes live in the git-ignored artifact tree and are digest-checked before the copy.
benchmark/godot-load-test/fox.glb
benchmark/godot-load-test/fox.glb.import
benchmark/godot-load-test/fox_0.png
benchmark/godot-load-test/fox_0.png.import
# The retention index is generated on demand from the citation scan (PRD-323). It derives from
# every benchmark/verification file and every PRD or script that cites one, so tracking it meant
# it restaled on nearly every doc edit and conflicted on concurrent branches. Read it with
# `tsx scripts/generate-retention-index.ts`; no gate compares a tracked copy.
docs/benchmark/SCREENSHOT-RETENTION.md
hosting/.data/
# A sweep archive is half evidence and half build output, and only the second half leaves git
# (PRD-323 Phase 4). The tree held 5,292 tracked files, of which 2,963 were generated arm `.ts`
# game sources — crossed by every repo-wide grep an agent runs, the same hazard the root
# `AGENTS.md` names for `.worktrees/` at five times the file count.
#
# **What stays is decided by what the suite reads, and the only instrument that answers that is a
# clean-tree run.** Two earlier attempts were wrong because they were checked on a machine that
# still had the files on disk. Ignoring the whole tree failed three suites in CI. Ignoring these
# four directories everywhere still failed two, because `sweep-delta.spec.ts` and
# `sweep-ledger.spec.ts` do not read the recorded measurement — they **recompute** it with
# `measureSandbox` and diff it against the committed record, which is the regression ratchet
# working as designed. `measure-sandbox.ts:306` needs the archive's `src/`, `:216` its frozen
# `starter-baseline/src/`, and `:102` the `framework-types/` declarations. `git ls-files` showing
# a tracked `proof.json` proves nothing about any of that.
#
# So the three measurable directories are **kept for the 13 archives a `docs/verification/sweep-*.md`
# ledger names** — 456 files, 374 `.ts`, 2.6 MB — and ignored for the other 94. Tracked `.ts` under
# `docs/` lands near 376 rather than 2,965: an 87% cut that keeps the ratchet honest. Making the
# specs compare a recorded manifest instead of re-measuring would reclaim the rest and weaken the
# ratchet, which is a worse trade.
#
# The verification is `git archive <sha> | tar -x` into an empty directory, symlink `node_modules`,
# and run `sweep-delta`, `sweep-ledger` and `capture` there. Nothing else counts.
#
# Every archive keeps its measurements either way: `sweep.json`, `proof.json`, `proof-artifacts/`,
# `playtests/`, `captures/`, `screenshots/`, `brief.md`, `reference.png`. The whole archive stays on
# disk, and every sweep command still resolves this tree through the filesystem, never through git.
#
# `**` rather than a bare directory, because git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is
# excluded — the negations below would silently do nothing against `.../src/`.
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/src/**
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/starter-baseline/**
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/framework-types/**
!docs/benchmark/sweeps/endless-runner-2026-08-05/src/**
!docs/benchmark/sweeps/endless-runner-2026-08-05/starter-baseline/**
!docs/benchmark/sweeps/endless-runner-2026-08-05/framework-types/**
!docs/benchmark/sweeps/endless-runner-2026-08-08-11/src/**
!docs/benchmark/sweeps/endless-runner-2026-08-08-11/starter-baseline/**
!docs/benchmark/sweeps/endless-runner-2026-08-08-11/framework-types/**
!docs/benchmark/sweeps/endless-runner-2026-08-08-6/src/**
