# Third-party models a sweep was handed as source material. The FPS kit's first-person viewmodel
# records "user-provided; verify upstream pack terms before redistribution" and its enemy is
# CC-BY-4.0 carrying retargeted Mixamo clips, so neither is ours to redistribute from an MIT
# repository. The archive keeps them on disk; git does not carry them.
# Generated sweep instruction files are not benchmark evidence; their proof records remain tracked.
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/AGENTS.md
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/CLAUDE.md
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/vendor/
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/assets/models/
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/assets/imported/
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/assets/generated/
# Builder session transcripts: the archived evidence a cold run happened, but ~8 MB of gzipped
# JSONL each carrying absolute paths from the machine that ran them. Commit one deliberately with
# `git add -f` if a result is disputed; do not carry every run's in history by default.
docs/benchmark/sweeps/*/transcript.jsonl.gz
.linchpin/
.gauntlet/

# Shared editor settings are committed — they keep VS Code's watcher and TypeScript server out
# of the 6+ GB of build output under packages/runtime-native. Everything else VS Code drops in
# here is per-machine and is not.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json

# Other agents' lanes. Never searched, never read; see AGENTS.md.
.worktrees
# The other half of the same rule (PRD-357 F1). The global worktree convention puts Claude Code's
# lanes in `<repo-root>/.claude/worktrees/`, and until 2026-09-04 the only thing keeping them out
# of a search was line 12 of `.git/info/exclude` — per-clone, untracked, hand-written on one
# machine. Every other clone's ripgrep crossed 629,652 files and stopped being the fast path.
# No trailing slash, matching `.worktrees` above, so `git check-ignore .claude/worktrees` resolves
# from this file even when the directory does not exist yet.
.claude/worktrees

# Secrets. Never committed, never copied into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# written by installing @threenative/core (workspace link writes it at the repo root too)
.mcp.json
# ...except the template copies, which are shipped source. The pattern above is unanchored, so it
# swallowed the config of every template added after it: the file generated fine, `git status` said
# nothing, and the scaffold shipped without it. That surfaced as four scaffold suites failing on
#   Error: Scaffold produced no .mcp.json at '.../puzzle/.mcp.json'
# for templates whose config was present on the author's disk the whole time.
!packages/create-threenative/templates/*/.mcp.json
/.codex/

# generated from packages/engine-mcp/dist during the core package build
packages/assets/dist/blender-gpl/

# Sandbox mini-game captures, left at the root for inspection. Not part of the repo.
screenshot-*.png

# `pnpm pack` output. Several gates pack the workspace into `packages/*.tgz` to install a
# scaffold the way a stranger's machine would; three of them were committed by accident in #37.
*.tgz

# Python bytecode caches. `packages/blender-mcp/gpl/recipes` is executed by Blender, which
# writes a `__pycache__` beside the recipes on every run; one .pyc was committed by accident.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

.afk/

# Local visual-iteration scaffolds and frames (scripts/shot.ts loop). Not part of the repo.
.tnshots/

